{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011CduYfhKwf6qQibiYixjsQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Quicksort picks a pivot element and partitions the array into two halves — elements less than the pivot, and elements greater — then recursively sorts each half in place.\n\n**Complexity:**\n- Average: O(n log n)\n- Worst case: O(n²) — occurs when the pivot is consistently the min or max (e.g., sorted input with naive pivot selection)\n- Space: O(log n) average (stack frames), vs mergesort's O(n)\n\n**Choose quicksort over mergesort when:**\n- You need in-place sorting (mergesort typically requires auxiliary space)\n- Cache performance matters — quicksort has better locality of reference\n- Average-case performance is acceptable and worst-case is mitigated (e.g., randomized pivot)\n\n**Choose mergesort when:**\n- You need guaranteed O(n log n) worst-case\n- Sorting linked lists (no random access needed)\n- Stability is required (equal elements must preserve original order)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9472,"cache_read_input_tokens":16933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9472},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5154cc3-3fd5-4610-aa76-a531000bca2d","uuid":"4aa27c93-7a3c-4b51-92a3-dda97b0f7b61","timestamp":"2026-08-10T18:32:47.878Z","request_id":"req_011CduYff7k9YKVkZaGG7ntL"}
